WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.425
So, four decisions.

2
00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:04.484
Name the planes and assets
that are expected to emit,

3
00:00:04.484 --> 00:00:07.400
and check each one against
what actually arrives.

4
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.808
Stand up the naming plane
before the evidence pipeline,

5
00:00:10.808 --> 00:00:13.475
so every record joins
on one asset identity.

6
00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:17.716
Fund the Agency Logging Plan as
the program's visibility plan,

7
00:00:17.716 --> 00:00:19.462
not as a storage purchase.

8
00:00:19.462 --> 00:00:25.006
And send every blind spot to the
authorizing official: a telemetry gap,

9
00:00:25.006 --> 00:00:31.124
a suppression with no end date, a missed
BOD 26-04 deadline, each with an end date.

10
00:00:31.124 --> 00:00:33.325
The next step needs no procurement.

11
00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:36.233
Run the coverage check
against the inventory,

12
00:00:36.233 --> 00:00:40.824
tag the exposure of every externally
reachable asset before December 7,

13
00:00:40.824 --> 00:00:44.650
and count a source as covered
only when a tested rule reads it.

14
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.813
You can't defend what you can't see,

15
00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:50.738
and a finding closes only when
the thing is fixed, with proof.

16
00:00:50.738 --> 00:00:54.425
Book 12 has the detail,
every claim footnoted.

17
00:00:54.425 --> 00:00:55.250
Thank you.
